### Requests for the JetBrains HTTP client (click the ▶ next to each one).
### Auth is by httpOnly cookies (access_token, refresh_token): run a login below first, the client keeps
### the cookies and sends them with every later request. One session at a time: log in as eva to act as eva.
### Seeded users (password password123): jan@example.test (trusted), eva@example.test (verified),
### petr@example.test (registered), blocked@example.test (blocked).
### Every POST/PATCH/DELETE needs the header X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest (CSRF check, 403 without it).
### Seed ids: set UkLWZ (children gbHJd, EfhxL), Obsah kruhu VqXmZ, Pythagorova věta uw2YK,
### Eva's private OIJLh, textbook problem AXs1i; chapter Rovnice UkLWZ; licence CC BY 4.0 gbHJd.

@base = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### ---- Auth ----

### Register a new teacher (also logs in: both cookies are set)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna@skola.cz", "username": "anna", "password": "tajne-heslo-123", "displayName": "Anna Nováková" }

### Log in as jan
POST {{base}}/auth/login
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jan@example.test", "password": "password123" }

### Log in as eva
POST {{base}}/auth/login
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "eva@example.test", "password": "password123" }

### Who am I (the web app calls this on startup)
GET {{base}}/auth/me

### Renew the session: rotates the refresh token. Sending the OLD one again revokes the whole chain.
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

### Log out (always 204, clears both cookies)
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

### Wrong password -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{base}}/auth/login
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jan@example.test", "password": "wrong" }

### Blocked account -> 403 ACCOUNT_BLOCKED (only after a correct password)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "blocked@example.test", "password": "password123" }

### No X-Requested-With header -> 403 CSRF_CHECK_FAILED
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jan@example.test", "password": "password123" }

### ---- Problems (log in as jan first) ----

### My problems (dashboard)
GET {{base}}/problems?scope=mine

### Public browser, filtered by chapter (includes child chapters)
GET {{base}}/problems?scope=public&chapterId=UkLWZ

### Detail of a set
GET {{base}}/problems/UkLWZ

### 2.0.0 flow: create problems one at a time, nest them in a set, reorder, take one out.
### Run the requests below in order; each one stores what the next needs (ids, lockVersion).

### 1. Create problem A
POST {{base}}/problems
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rovnice a)", "assignment": "\( 2x + 3 = 11 \)", "result": "\( x = 4 \)" }

> {% client.global.set("a", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Create problem B
POST {{base}}/problems
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rovnice b)", "assignment": "\( x^2 = 9 \)", "result": "\( x = \pm 3 \)" }

> {% client.global.set("b", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Create the set parent (no result: a set parent must not have one)
POST {{base}}/problems
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Řešte rovnice", "assignment": "Vyřešte rovnice v oboru reálných čísel:", "tagIds": ["UkLWZ"], "chapterIds": ["UkLWZ"] }

> {% client.global.set("set", response.body.id); client.global.set("lock", response.body.lockVersion); %}

### 4. Add A to the set by MOVE (your own private problem; same record)
POST {{base}}/problems/{{set}}/children
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lockVersion": {{lock}}, "problemId": "{{a}}" }

> {% client.global.set("lock", response.body.lockVersion); %}

### 5. Add a foreign problem (Pythagorova věta) by COPY, as the first child (afterId null)
POST {{base}}/problems/{{set}}/children
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lockVersion": {{lock}}, "copyFromId": "uw2YK", "afterId": null }

> {% client.global.set("copy", response.body.children[0].id); client.global.set("lock", response.body.lockVersion); %}

### 6. Add B by move, right after A (afterId = A)
POST {{base}}/problems/{{set}}/children
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lockVersion": {{lock}}, "problemId": "{{b}}", "afterId": "{{a}}" }

> {% client.global.set("lock", response.body.lockVersion); %}

### 7. Reorder: move the copy to the end (afterId = the current last child, B)
PATCH {{base}}/problems/{{set}}/children/{{copy}}
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lockVersion": {{lock}}, "afterId": "{{b}}" }

> {% client.global.set("lock", response.body.lockVersion); %}

### 8. Take A out of the set (the lock travels in If-Match; A becomes a standalone private problem)
DELETE {{base}}/problems/{{set}}/children/{{a}}
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
If-Match: "{{lock}}"

> {% client.global.set("lock", response.body.lockVersion); %}

### Copy a published problem (log in as eva)
POST {{base}}/problems/VqXmZ/copy
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

### Publish the set with a licence (log in as jan)
POST {{base}}/problems/UkLWZ/publish
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Content-Type: application/json

{ "licenseId": "gbHJd" }

### Dissolve a set (children become standalone)
POST {{base}}/problems/UkLWZ/dissolve
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

